# The lmgw source the sidebar page (sidebar/, design §8.2, §10) is built against: lmgw-chat-ui,
# lmgw-ui-kit, lmgw-api-types and lmgw-client, plus lmgw-ui's base stylesheet and its fonts. Three
# lines that name the same source, as in Kai's LMGW_PIN:
#   lmgw_commit  the commit in lmgw's development history: the checkout next to this repository
#                locally, GitLab CI's clone
#   lmgw_tag     the published lmgw release (github.com/lmgw-dev/lmgw) whose tree is lmgw_tree, which
#                the GitHub release workflow clones, or `unpublished` while no release has that tree
#                yet (the workflow then fails and says so)
#   lmgw_tree    the commit's tree: the public repository gets one squashed commit per publish, with
#                other commit hashes but the same tree, so the tree is what every build stages from
# `scripts/lmgw-pin.sh stage` copies the crates out of the pinned tree (git archive) into
# target/lmgw-pin/, where sidebar/Cargo.toml finds them; the checkout itself is only read.
